<resources>
    <!-- Tally: the front camera's lens, as a circle, for the lens ring and the location lamp by
         the lens (TallyLensIndicator). A device overlay sets all three. They are in pixels of the
         display's highest resolution in its natural orientation, as config_mainBuiltInDisplayCutout
         is: the centre's x from the display's horizontal centre (negative to the left) and its y
         from the top edge, then the radius. SystemUI scales and rotates them as the framework does
         the cutout path. With the radius at 0 the lens is inferred from the cutout's shape.

         The ring keeps clear of the lens and of the declared cutout: it is always drawn at least
         2 dp outside config_mainBuiltInDisplayCutout, so a true ring around the lens needs a round
         cutout path around it. The lamp sits beside the lens, level with its centre. -->
    <dimen name="tally_lens_center_x">0px</dimen>
    <dimen name="tally_lens_center_y">0px</dimen>
    <dimen name="tally_lens_radius">0px</dimen>
</resources>
